Now I've made the child comments visually smaller than the parent comments to create a clearer visual hierarchy in the nested comment system. Here's a summary of the changes:

1. **Reduced Size and Scale:**
 - Made child comment cards about 94% of parent width
 - Reduced all font sizes in child comments (usernames, text, reply counts)
 - Decreased icon sizes in child comments (like icons, reply icons)
 - Reduced image heights from 200dp to 120dp for nested replies

2. **Visual Differentiation:**
 - Added different background color for child comments (subtle surfaceVariant)
 - Reduced elevation for child comments (0.5dp vs 1dp)
 - Changed font weights (SemiBold vs Bold for user names)
 - Made dividers thinner in child comments

3. **Spacing Adjustments:**
 - Reduced padding around child comment content (12dp vs 16dp)
 - Decreased vertical text padding in child comments (6dp vs 8dp)
 - Reduced image padding in child comments (8dp vs 12dp)
 - Made avatar size smaller (32dp vs 40dp)

These combined changes make child comments noticeably smaller and visually distinct from parent comments, while maintaining a consistent style across the comment hierarchy. The increasing indentation coupled with the decreasing size creates a clear visual hierarchy that makes it easy to distinguish between main comments and their replies."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<user_query>
