I've updated the keyboard behavior in the CommentScreen to keep the top navigation bar and post details visible when the keyboard appears. Here's what I've added:

1. **Proper Inset Handling:**
 - Added `imePadding()` to the input card to ensure it stays above the keyboard
 - Added `navigationBarsPadding()` to handle system navigation bars
 - Maintained a consistent bottom padding for the scrollable content

2. **Scrolling Behavior Enhancement:**
 - Added a `LazyColumn` with a `rememberLazyListState()` for better scroll control
 - Created a `LaunchedEffect` that intelligently scrolls content when replying to comments
 - Ensured the UI doesn't jump around when the keyboard appears/disappears

3. **Focus Management:**
 - Fixed focus control when replying to comments
 - Cleared focus when needed to improve keyboard behavior
 - Added proper focus transitions between comments

4. **Visual Improvements:**
 - Ensured the comment input card has proper surface color matching the theme
 - Applied proper elevation to make the input area stand out
 - Maintained visual consistency throughout keyboard transitions

With these changes, when you tap to reply to a comment:
1. The keyboard will appear without pushing the top navigation off-screen
2. The post details will remain visible at the top
3. The view will automatically scroll to show the relevant comment context
4. The input box will position itself properly above the keyboard

This creates a much better user experience where the context remains visible while commenting, which is especially important in a discussion thread."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<user_query>
