+
+1. Install Node.js if you haven't already
+2. Install Firebase Admin SDK: `npm install firebase-admin`
+3. Download your service account key:
+ - Go to Firebase Console > Project Settings > Service Accounts
+ - Click "Generate new private key"
+ - Save the JSON file as `serviceAccountKey.json` in the same folder as the script
+4. Run the script: `node delete_firebase_data.js`
+
+## Setting up a new Cloudinary account
+
+1. Sign up for a new Cloudinary account at [cloudinary.com](https://cloudinary.com)
+2. Get your new Cloud Name from the dashboard
+3. Create a new upload preset:
+ - Go to Settings > Upload
+ - Scroll to Upload presets
+ - Click "Add upload preset"
+ - Set signing mode to "Unsigned"
+ - Save the preset name
+4. Update your app with the new values:
+ - Open `app/src/main/java/com/example/kiendatn2/MyApplication.kt`
+ - Replace `CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME` with your new cloud name
+ - Replace `CLOUDINARY_UPLOAD_PRESET` with your new upload preset name
