Now you can use the enhanced MediaPicker in your application. Here's a summary of the changes made:

1. Modified the MediaPicker component to:
 - Support both images and videos through the `includeVideos` parameter
 - Show a play icon overlay on video thumbnails
 - Return whether the selected media is a video or not
 - Renamed MediaImage to MediaItem with an isVideo property

2. Added new string resources:
 - "select_media" - For when including both images and videos
 - "no_media_found" - For when no media files are found

3. Updated PostScreen to:
 - Use the enhanced MediaPicker component
 - Request appropriate permissions for both images and videos
 - Provide a proper bottom sheet for media selection

4. Updated ProfileScreen to:
 - Use the enhanced MediaPicker component with includeVideos=false
 - Pass the updated callback signature

Now users can select both images and videos in the post creation flow, while the profile picture selection is restricted to images only. The MediaPicker handles all the querying, permissions, and preview functionality in a consistent way across both screens."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<user_query>
