I've fixed the search screen implementation. Here are the key improvements:

1. Removed unnecessary debug logs which were cluttering the code
2. Simplified the UI structure for better organization
3. Made search history display consistent regardless of search state
4. Fixed the SearchHistorySection to properly handle empty states
5. Improved the layout of search history items for better usability

Now the search functionality works as follows:
- User enters a query in the search box
- When search button is clicked or keyboard search action is triggered, the query is saved to Firebase
- Search history is displayed at the bottom of the screen
- Users can click on a history item to repeat that search
- Users can delete individual history items or clear their entire search history
- The search query is populated in the search box when a history item is clicked

All Firebase integrations remain intact - searches are saved to the searchHistory collection, and the user can manage their search history as needed."}]}]}

