Great! I've successfully updated the app to respect post visibility restrictions. Here's a summary of the changes made:

1. The Post data class now includes a `visibility` field with three options:
 - `PUBLIC`: Post can be seen by anyone
 - `FRIENDS_ONLY`: Post can only be seen by the author and their friends
 - `PRIVATE`: Post can only be seen by the author

2. Added a helper method `getFriendUserIds()` to get the list of a user's friends

3. Updated the key repository methods to filter posts based on visibility:
 - `getPostsWithLikeStatus()`: Shows posts based on visibility rules
 - `getFriendsPostsWithLikeStatus()`: Shows only public and friends-only posts from friends
 - `searchPosts()`: Only includes posts the user is allowed to see based on visibility
 - `getPostById()`: Respects visibility restrictions when fetching a single post

4. Fixed the UI to display the appropriate visibility icons next to usernames in post details

With these changes, the post visibility feature is now fully implemented. Users can choose the visibility level when creating posts, and the system will ensure that only authorized users can see restricted posts."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<additional_data>
