The changes I've made ensure that when a user clicks the search button:

1. The search query is first saved to Firebase using `saveSearchToHistory`
2. Then the search is performed using `searchPosts`
3. The search history is automatically loaded when:
 - The screen is first opened (via the LaunchedEffect)
 - After a search query is saved (via loadSearchHistory in saveSearchToHistory)
 - When the user clears the search field (via the clear button)
4. Search history can be:
 - Displayed when no active search is in progress
 - Clicked to reuse a previous search
 - Individually deleted
 - Completely cleared

The changes prioritize saving the query before performing the search, and ensures proper refresh of the search history. I've also moved the search history UI components to a separate file for better code organization."}]}]}

{"id":"94f4e3dc-0932-459b-a10b-ed71d235fa89","name":"Adding Share Functionality to Social Media App in Jetpack Compose","timestamp":1746986162307,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<user_query>
Please carefully analyze my social media app codebase, which is built using Jetpack Compose. Your task is to add a share function with the following specifications:

Functionality:

The share function will allow users to share a post.

When a post is shared, the name of the user who shared it should appear at the top of the post item, specifically above the author's profile picture.

The format should be:

X (user) shared a post

The shared post will appear only in the friends' post tab.

The post will not reload for the you's tab, but the friends' tab should reload to reflect the shared post.

Implementation:

