After thorough investigation and multiple fixes, I've completely redesigned the share button implementation to ensure it clearly shows when a post is shared:

1. Created a specialized ShareButton component with distinct visual states:
 - When shared: Pink background with white text and icon
 - When not shared: Bordered button with regular text color

2. Fixed several issues in the implementation:
 - Replaced the original tinting approach (which wasn't working reliably)
 - Added extensive debug logging to track state changes
 - Simplified the component structure for better reliability
 - Used hardcoded colors to avoid theme issues
 - Made the shared state much more visually distinct

3. Improved the state management:
 - Added more reliable state tracking
 - Enhanced the visual feedback for state changes
 - Added debug logs at every step

The share button should now show a completely different appearance when shared (pink background with white text) versus not shared (bordered button with regular text), making it impossible to miss when it's in the shared state.

