Now I've implemented the restriction that private posts can only be shared with the "Only Me" option. Here's what has been added:

1. In the `FirebaseRepository`, I added a check that prevents sharing a private post with friends (non-private sharing).

2. In the `PostItemDetailed` component, I disabled the "Share (For friends)" menu option if the post has a private visibility setting.

3. In the `PostViewModel`, I added error handling that provides feedback when sharing fails due to attempting to share a private post with friends.

These changes ensure that:
- Users can still repost private posts for their own viewing (with the "Only Me" option)
- The UI clearly indicates when a post cannot be shared with friends (the option is disabled)
- If someone tries to circumvent the UI restrictions programmatically, the backend will still prevent the action and provide an error message

Private posts will remain private, even when shared or reposted."}]}]}

